## 📊 Quick Revision Summary

### EC2 Key Points:
```
✅ EC2 = Virtual Servers in AWS Cloud
✅ AMI = Template to launch instances
✅ Security Group = Firewall (stateful)
✅ NACL = Subnet-level firewall (stateless)
✅ EBS = Persistent storage
✅ Instance Store = Temporary storage
✅ Elastic IP = Static public IP
✅ Auto Scaling = Automatic capacity management
✅ Placement Groups = Physical placement control
✅ User Data = Bootstrap script on first launch
```

### RDS Blue/Green Key Points:
```
🔵 Blue = Current Production (stable)
🟢 Green = Staging Copy (for changes)
✅ Replication = Binlog/Logical (near real-time)
✅ Switchover = Under 60 seconds
✅ Endpoint = Stays the same after switchover
✅ Rollback = Blue retained until you delete it
✅ Supported = MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, Aurora
❌ Not Supported = SQL Server, Cross-Region
```

